# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# What the store held when this boot began, whether a file of the tree came back, and the line the
# run before left in /private/var/mobile: a line with an earlier second is that boot's volume coming
# back. Then this run's own line, and the file again a minute later.
#
# The marker lives under mobile/, not at the root of the volume: a name made in the root of the
# ramfs cannot be looked up again afterwards (stamp creates it and reports the bytes, and the next
# open of the same path answers ENOENT), while everything iOS keeps lives in subdirectories and
# comes back through them. Nothing here saves: the job com.redwood.varstore does, when the kernel
# says the run is ending.
/redwood/bin/var_store show
/redwood/bin/var_store cat /private/var/root/Library/MobileContainerManager/containers.sqlite3 16
/redwood/bin/var_store cat /private/var/mobile/redwood-stamp 256
/redwood/bin/var_store cat /private/var/mobile/Library/Preferences/.GlobalPreferences.plist 96
/redwood/bin/var_store stamp /private/var/mobile/redwood-stamp
sleep 60
/redwood/bin/var_store cat /private/var/mobile/redwood-stamp 256
/redwood/bin/var_store show
